ty, North York, United States."}]}}, {"fullName": "Trivedi H", "lastName": "Trivedi", "firstName": "Hari", "initials": "H", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-6648-8334"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Radiology, Emory University, Atlanta, United States."}]}}, {"fullName": "Purkayastha S", "lastName": "Purkayastha", "firstName": "Saptarshi", "initials": "S", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3625-534X"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "School of Informatics and Computing, Indiana University Purdue University, Indianapolis, United States."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-6648-8334"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3327-8004"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3625-534X"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1150", "volume": "96", "journalIssueId": 3669394, "dateOfPublication": "2023 Oct", "monthOfPublication": 10, "yearOfPublication": 2023, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Br J Radiol", "title": "The British journal of radiology", "essn": "1748-880X", "issn": "0007-1285", "nlmid": "0373125", "isoabbreviation": "Br J Radiol"}, "printPublicationDate": "2023-10-01"}, "pubYear": "2023", "pageInfo": "20230023", "abstractText": "Various forms of artificial intelligence (AI) applications are being deployed and used in many healthcare systems. As the use of these applications increases, we are learning the failures of these models and how they can perpetuate bias. With these new lessons, we need to prioritize bias evaluation and mitigation for radiology applications; all the while not ignoring the impact of changes in the larger enterprise AI deployment which may have downstream impact on performance of AI models. In this paper, we provide an updated review of known pitfalls causing AI bias and discuss strategies for mitigating these biases within the context of AI deployment in the larger healthcare enterprise. We describe these pitfalls by framing them in the larger AI lifecycle from problem definition, data set selection and curation, model training and deployment emphasizing that bias exists across a spectrum and is a sequela of a combination of both human and machine factors.", "affiliation": "Department of Radiology, Emory University, Atlanta, United States.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["review-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NHLBI NIH HHS", "acronym": "HL", "grantId": "75N92020C00008", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NHLBI NIH HHS", "acronym": "HL", "grantId": "75N92020C00021", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIBIB NIH HHS", "acronym": "EB", "grantId": "R01 EB017205", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Disease Progression"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Learning"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Radiology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Artificial Intelligence"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Bias"}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1259/bjr.20230023"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10546443"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10546443?pdf=render"}]}, "isOpenAccess": "Y", "inEPMC": "Y", "inPMC": "Y", "citedByCount": 130, "hasReferences": "Y", "hasTextMinedTerms": "Y", "hasDbCrossReferences": "N",